<DocsPage slug="deployment">
  <h1>Deployment options</h1>
  <p class="lpd-sub">
    LACE runs in four footprints. The governance substrate — permissions,
    evidence, budgets, approvals, audit — is identical in every one of them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="footprints">Footprints</h2>
  <div class="lpd-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Footprint</th><th>Where it runs</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Managed cloud</strong></td><td>Our cloud</td><td>Fastest start; usage-based AI budgets with hard caps.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Private cloud</strong></td><td>Your VPC</td><td>SSO/OIDC, custom connectors, BYO models.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>On-premises</strong></td><td>Your data center</td><td>Full platform, your hardware and boundary.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Air-gapped</strong></td><td>Disconnected enclave</td><td>No external AI calls; accreditation evidence exportable.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="air-gapped">Air-gapped deployment</h2>
  <p>
    Air-gapped is not a configuration flag over a cloud product. Model serving,
    embedding, indexing, and orchestration all run inside the boundary on
    open-weight models you host, so no code path requires an outbound
    connection to function — including model and platform updates, which are
    applied from media you control.
  </p>
  <p>
    Programs with an accreditation requirement should also read
    <a href="/applications/lace-gov">LACE-GOV</a>, which packages the platform
    with BFO/CCO schema packs, cross-enclave federation, and exportable
    accreditation evidence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="models">Model choice</h2>
  <p>
    Every footprint supports bringing your own models. Managed cloud can use
    hosted frontier models under budget caps; private cloud, on-premises, and
    air-gapped deployments serve open-weight models on your hardware. Because
    enforcement lives outside the model, changing the model does not change what
    the platform will let it do.
  </p>
</DocsPage>
